    {
      "id": "Logic.cxmp.nat-add-not-defeq",
      "package": "_unpackaged",
      "kind": "counterexample",
      "title": {
        "en": "Commutativity of Natural-Number Addition Is Not Definitional Equality",
        "zh-CN": "自然数加法交换律不是依定义相等"
      },
      "content": {
        "markdown": {
          "en": "In the metatheory of untyped $\\lambda$-calculus, let $m,n$ be variables standing for natural-number expressions. The open expressions $\\mathsf{add}\\;m\\;n$ and $\\mathsf{add}\\;n\\;m$ are generally not definitionally equal. This concerns expressions, not closed expressions obtained by substituting concrete Church numerals; the latter both $\\beta$-reduce to the same Church numeral.",
          "zh-CN": "在无类型 $\\lambda$-演算的元理论中，令 $m,n$ 为表示自然数表达式的变量。开放表达式 $\\mathsf{add}\\;m\\;n$ 与 $\\mathsf{add}\\;n\\;m$ 一般不是依定义相等的。这讨论的是表达式，而不是代入具体丘奇数后得到的闭表达式；后两者都可通过 $\\beta$-归约得到同一个丘奇数。"
        }
      },
      "parent_entry_id": "Logic.subsec.propositional",
      "parent_node_ids": [
        "n_sub_prop"
      ],
      "after_entry_id": "Logic.def.iff",
      "graph_level": "entry"
    },
    {
      "id": "Type.cxmp.vector-index-not-defeq",
      "package": "TypeTheory",
      "kind": "counterexample",
      "title": {
        "en": "Commutativity of Vector Indices Is Not Definitional Equality",
        "zh-CN": "向量下标的交换律不是依定义相等"
      },
      "content": {
        "markdown": {
          "en": "In CIC, for variable natural-number indices $m,n$, the types $\\operatorname{Vector}(m+n)$ and $\\operatorname{Vector}(n+m)$ are generally not definitionally equal. Commutativity of addition gives a propositional equality, so transporting or rewriting along that proof is required.",
          "zh-CN": "在 CIC 中，对于作为变量的自然数下标 $m,n$，类型 $\\operatorname{Vector}(m+n)$ 与 $\\operatorname{Vector}(n+m)$ 一般不是依定义相等的。加法交换律给出的是命题相等，因此需要沿该证明进行转运或改写。"
        }
      },
      "parent_entry_id": "Type.def.vector",
      "parent_node_ids": [
        "n_54"
      ],
      "after_entry_id": "Type.def.vector.recursor",
      "graph_level": "subentry"
    }
  ],
